      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Venom arrived during horror's exploration of regional American folklore and superstition. While <a href=\"/movie/2667\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"2667\">The Blair Witch Project</a> (1999) mined Northeastern mythology and <a href=\"/movie/10212\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"10212\">Ravenous</a> (1999) tackled frontier cannibalism, Southern Gothic horror experienced a renaissance with films like <a href=\"/movie/2662\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"2662\">House of 1000 Corpses</a> (2003) and <a href=\"/movie/19592\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"19592\">Dead Birds</a> (2004) mixing regional history with supernatural horror."
      }
